    "identifier": "hozuki-water-blob",
    "description": "<p>A target creature you can see within range must make a Dexterity saving throw, having only their head submerged in a bubble of water, made from your body. For the duration of this jutsu, while a creatures head is submerged in this way, they are suffocating. While suffocating, it is difficult to maintain concentration on jutsu as they must spend the original cost of the jutsu to maintain concentration while suffocating. A suffocating creature takes 4d8 necrotic damage at the end of each of their turns. This damage cannot be reduced or ignored.</p>\n<p>Affected creature can remake their saving throw at the end of each of their turns, to end this jutsu’s effect on them.</p>\n<p>Hydrofication. This jutsu’s range becomes 30 Feet.</p>",
